    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0497" n="389" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg389"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/577: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-05-18T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 18, 1927—10
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 18—1:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>568. My 137, February 12, 4 p.m. Following from American consul at Hankow: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“May 16, 11 a.m. One percent surtax on imports and exports for dike
                            construction was deferred but is now being imposed, having become
                            effective May 10th, collections being made independent of Customs and in
                            the same manner in which two and a half percent surtax. Five percent
                            surtax on luxuries, list of which is being mailed,<anchor n="43"
                                xml:id="d439-f1"/> is being collected also.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
